outcome failure
file Makefile kept 18
| # The filed reproducer: an environment MAKEFLAGS is makefile TEXT, expanded
| # before it is split into switches.
| #
| # GNU Make's `decode_env_switches` (main.c) builds `$(MAKEFLAGS)`, hands it to
| # `variable_expand`, and only then splits the result into words. So the value
| # `$(subst X,-,Xk)` decodes to `-k` — a reader that never expands it dies on
| # `invalid option -- '$'` instead.
| #
| # The `-k` is the whole point of the case: with the stream expanded, `good`
| # still runs after `bad` fails and `kept-going` is written; without it the
| # build stops at the first failure and the file is never there.
| all: bad good
| 
| bad:
| 	@exit 1
| 
| good:
| 	@printf 'the stream expanded to -k\n' > kept-going
file kept-going touched 1
| the stream expanded to -k
